t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Yesterday, President Donald J. Trump</strong> <a href=\"https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/national-cyber-director-sean-cairncross-leaving-kirsten-davies-replaci-rcna610329\"><strong>named</strong></a> <strong>Kirsten A. Davies to lead the White House Office of the National Cyber Director.</strong> A battle-tested cyber leader and the Pentagon’s Chief Information Officer, Davies will drive an America First cyber strategy that treats cybersecurity as national security and keeps the United States dominant and secure in cyberspace.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Her selection immediately drew praise from leaders across the Administration:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://x.com/SecRubio/status/2123591426814460410\">Secretary of State Marco Rubio</a>: “Congratulations to the new National Cyber Director Kirsten Davies — look forward to working together to strengthen America’s cybersecurity.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://x.com/SecWar/status/2123594274721644701\">Secretary of War Pete Hegseth</a>: “The Department congratulates Kirsten Davies on her new role as the National Cyber Director. Throughout her tenure at DOW, she has proven herself to be a dedicated patriot and professional, and we are confident she will advance President Trump’s America First agenda across the cybersecurity landscape.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123598853639119139\">Director of National Intelligence Jay Clayton</a>: “With nearly two decades of leadership experience in the technology space, Kirsten Davies will be a strong asset for the Trump administration in her new position with the Office of the National Cyber Director. It has been my pleasure to work closely with Kirsten on national security matters, and I look forward to now working with her to navigate an increasingly dynamic and fast-moving cyber landscape.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://x.com/mkratsios47/status/2123618337133314072\">Director of the Office of Science and Technology Policy Michael Kratsios</a>: “Congratulations @_KirstenDavies_, our new National Cyber Director. Kirsten brings deep cyber expertise and a proven record from her time in industry and at the Department of War. Cybersecurity is vital to our nation’s security and prosperity, and I look forward to working together to strengthen it.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://x.com/ajtata/status/2123603655496454271\">Under Secretary of War for Personnel and Readiness Anthony Tata</a>: “Great pick. Congrats @_KirstenDavies_. Look forward to continuing to work together.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://x.com/MarciMcCarthyUS/status/2123606115737112967?a=PI6lkScY-HwaHjiYd6g&amp;s=20\">Director of External Engagements for the Department of War CIO Marci McCarthy</a>: “Congratulations, @Kirsten_Davies_! Having worked alongside you, I’ve witnessed firsthand your extraordinary leadership, vision, and unwavering commitment to strengthening our nation’s cybersecurity and national security. Proud to call you both my boss and my great friend. America’s cyber future is in great hands!”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://x.com/HostileSpectrum/status/2123601171944268274?a=NuEfscUlobQlkgQZEc8&amp;s=20\">National Defense University Cyber Scholar JD Work</a>: “Congratulations. A superb choice for many reasons, foremost in technical excellence and deep executive competence solving for some of the hardest problems ever faced in the cyber domain.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump has made cybersecurity a core pillar of his Administration. Under his leadership, the United States has:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/03/white-house-unveils-president-trumps-cyber-strategy-for-america/\">Released</a> a Cyber Strategy for America built on six pillars to keep the United States unrivaled in cyberspace, on offense and defense;</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2026/06/national-security-presidential-memorandum-nspm-12/\">Overhauled</a> cybersecurity for America’s military and intelligence systems, holding agency heads accountable and modernizing oversight for the first time in over 35 years;</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/justice-department-and-fbi-seize-platforms-operated-and-used-china-state-sponsored-hackers\">Seized</a> Chinese state-sponsored hacking platforms targeting U.S. critical infrastructure, including NASA and the Federal Reserve;</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2026/08/expanding-capabilities-to-combat-transnational-cyber-enabled-crime/\">Unleashed</a> vetted American companies, under federal oversight, to go after foreign cybercriminal networks;</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2026/06/securing-the-nation-against-advanced-cryptographic-attacks/\">Mandated</a> post-quantum cryptography for high-value federal systems by 2030;</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2026/06/promoting-advanced-artificial-intelligence-innovation-and-security/\">Harnessed</a> AI to defend federal and military networks, creating a clearinghouse to find and patch vulnerabilities;</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2026/03/combating-cybercrime-fraud-and-predatory-schemes-against-american-citizens/\">Ordered</a> a plan to dismantle the transnational criminal networks and scam centers preying on Americans;</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/justice-department-charges-12-chinese-contract-hackers-and-law-enforcement-officers-global\">Charged</a> 12 Chinese contract hackers and law enforcement officers behind global hacking campaigns that hit U.S. agencies;</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Sanctioned ransomware enablers <a href=\"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/sb0559\">First VPN</a>, <a href=\"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/sb0319\">Media Land</a>, <a href=\"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/sb0185\">Aeza Group</a>, and <a href=\"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/sb0018\">Zservers</a>;</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.fcc.gov/document/fcc-updates-covered-list-include-foreign-made-consumer-routers\">Blocked</a> new foreign-made consumer routers deemed a national security threat;</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/06/sustaining-select-efforts-to-strengthen-the-nations-cybersecurity-and-amending-executive-order-13694-and-executive-order-14144/\">Hardened</a> federal software, internet routing, and encryption standards against foreign threats;</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Signed laws <a href=\"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/7147/all-info\">funding</a> the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency, <a href=\"https://therecord.media/trump-signs-ndaa-cyber-command\">authorizing</a> Cyber Command operations, and <a href=\"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/guidance-assist-non-federal-entities-share-cyber-threat-indicators-and-defensive-measures-federal\">extending</a> legal protections for companies that share cyber threat intelligence; and</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Taken decisive first-term action, <a href=\"https://trumpwhitehouse.archives.gov/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/National-Cyber-Strategy.pdf\">releasing</a> the first fully articulated national cyber strategy in 15 years, <a href=\"https://trumpwhitehouse.archives.gov/briefings-statements/statement-president-donald-j-trump-elevation-cyber-command/\">elevating</a> U.S. Cyber Command, <a href=\"https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2018/11/19/cybersecurity-and-infrastructure-security-agency\">creating</a> CISA, <a href=\"https://trumpwhitehouse.archives.gov/presidential-actions/executive-order-securing-information-communications-technology-services-supply-chain/\">securing</a> the tech supply chain from foreign adversaries, <a href=\"https://trumpwhitehouse.archives.gov/briefings-statements/president-donald-j-trump-committed-safeguarding-americas-vital-communications-networks-securing-5g-technology/\">ripping out</a> untrusted telecom equipment, and <a href=\"https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-17-01-removal-kaspersky-branded-products\">purging</a> untrusted software from federal systems.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/11/president-trump-taps-pentagon-cyber-chief-kirsten-davies-as-national-cyber-director/\">President Trump Taps Pentagon Cyber Chief Kirsten Davies as National Cyber Director</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
